<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conn Bacach O'Neill</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1480–1559</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conn Bacach O'Neill was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tir-eoghain">Tír Eoghain</a> from 1519 and the first Earl of Tyrone. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s policy of surrender and regrant he submitted in 1542, gave up the title of The O'Neill and received an English earldom. A dispute over the succession between his named heir Matthew and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shane-oneill">Shane O'Neill</a> drove him from power, and he died in the Pale in 1559.</p></div>
